Sound: digital effects through AudioDxe (EFI_AUDIO_IO_PROTOCOL).
 - new efi/i_hdasound.c: 16-channel software mixer (vanilla volume /
   separation / pitch) into 44.1 kHz 16-bit stereo, streamed through one
   long buffer kept two blocks ahead of the driver DMA (~90 ms latency),
   started on the first effect and stopped after a second of silence
 - replaces the old one-playback-per-effect code (which libsamplerate
   resampled per effect and could only play one at a time) and the
   interactive output prompt (getchar/scanf) that stalled startup
 - PC speaker remains the fallback; -pcspeaker forces it

